### Food Delivery Platform - AI MCP client (the chatbot's backend-for-frontend)
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
###
### The browser only talks to this service (through the API Gateway: /api/v1/assistant/**).
### It takes who you are from your access token (signed by user-service, checked with its public key), keeps the
### conversation in Redis, limits questions per user and calls ai-mcp-server (the LLM) with the same token.
### Start user-service, Redis, ai-mcp-server (and Ollama) first.
###
### Caller identity: Authorization: Bearer <accessToken of step 1>. A token lives 15 minutes (run step 1 again), and the
### assistant refuses one with less than 3 minutes left (401: an answer can take up to 150 s). X-User-* headers alone
### are not accepted any more.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@service = http://localhost:8097
@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}


### 1. Sign-ins -> access tokens
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}", "role": "CUSTOMER" }

###
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}", "role": "PLATFORM_ADMIN" }


### ============================ CHATBOT ============================

### 2. Is the assistant available? (never an error status)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/status

### 3. Starter questions for the role
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/suggestions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 4. Ask a question (new conversation: conversationId null). A CPU model can take a minute.
# @name chat
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": null, "message": "I want to order a biryani" }

### 5. Continue the same conversation
@conversationId = {{chat.response.body.$.conversationId}}

POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}", "message": "Show restaurants near my saved address" }

### 6. Restore the conversation after a page reload (your own conversation only)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/conversation?conversationId={{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 7. "New chat"
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/conversation?conversationId={{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ============================ ORDER BUTTONS ============================
### When a reply has a pendingAction, the screen shows Confirm / Cancel. Set actionId from that reply.

@actionId = replace-with-pendingAction-id

### 8. Confirm (pressing it twice returns ALREADY_CREATED, never a second order)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 9. Cancel
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ============================ CHECKS ============================

### 10. Admin suggestions
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/suggestions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 11. Identity headers without a token name nobody -> 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/suggestions
X-User-Id: 1
X-User-Role: PLATFORM_ADMIN

### 12. No token -> 401 (WWW-Authenticate: Bearer)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/assistant/suggestions

### 13. Direct call, bypassing the gateway
GET {{service}}/actuator/health
